@page "/mcp-server"

@* Describes the MCP server this demo's host maps at /mcp. Its route differs from the endpoint's on
   purpose: two literal endpoints on /mcp would make a GET of it ambiguous. *@

<PageTitle>MCP server - bit Balette</PageTitle>

<h1>MCP server</h1>

<p class="page-intro">
    This site hosts a Model Context Protocol server at <code>/mcp</code>, so an AI agent adding a command palette with
    Bit.Balette reads the library itself - its compiled API documentation, its guide, its stylesheet's variables, its
    real matcher and these demo pages - instead of guessing at an API it half remembers. Every tool is read-only.
</p>

<div class="panel padded">
    <h2>Connect a client</h2>

    <p>
        The endpoint is plain Streamable HTTP, so any MCP client connects with a URL and nothing else. The same tools
        are also served, version by version, through the bit platform's own server at
        <code>https://bitplatform.dev/mcp</code>, next to the other bit libraries.
    </p>

    <pre class="output"><code>@ClientConfig</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="panel padded">
    <h2>Tools</h2>

    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr><th>Tool</th><th>What it answers</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><code>SearchBalette</code></td>
                <td>Everything at once - the guide, every public member, the theme variables, the setup guides and the demo sources - each hit with the exact follow-up call.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>GetBaletteSetupGuide</code></td>
                <td>The complete wiring for one render mode: server, wasm, auto, standalone-wasm or hybrid.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>GetBaletteGuideSection</code></td>
                <td>One section of the reference guide, or the index of sections.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>GetBaletteApi</code></td>
                <td>One public type with every parameter, property and method, its real default and its documentation - or the index of types.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>GetBaletteThemeVariables</code></td>
                <td>Every <code>--bit-balette-*</code> custom property with its light and dark value, and the <code>data-balette</code> attributes to style an unstyled palette by.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>InspectBaletteSearch</code></td>
                <td>Runs the library's own matcher and ranker over a query and a list of commands, and reports each score, the highlighted positions and the final order.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>GetBaletteSourceFile</code></td>
                <td>One demo or library file verbatim - every page here is a working palette feature - or the index of files.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <p>
        The guide, the API, the theme variables and the sources are also exposed as <code>balette://</code> resources,
        and three prompts - <code>add-balette-to-app</code>, <code>implement-balette-feature</code> and
        <code>debug-balette-palette</code> - walk an agent through the common jobs in the right order.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="panel padded">
    <h2>The same tools over plain HTTP</h2>

    <p>
        Every tool is also a <code>GET</code> under <code>/api/mcp/...</code>: open one in a browser tab to read
        exactly what an agent is handed.
    </p>

    <ul>
        <li><a href="/api/mcp/SearchBalette?query=nested%20page%20prompt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/api/mcp/SearchBalette?query=nested page prompt</a></li>
        <li><a href="/api/mcp/GetBaletteApi?typeName=Balette" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/api/mcp/GetBaletteApi?typeName=Balette</a></li>
        <li><a href="/api/mcp/GetBaletteThemeVariables" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/api/mcp/GetBaletteThemeVariables</a></li>
        <li><a href="/api/mcp/InspectBaletteSearch?query=rc" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/api/mcp/InspectBaletteSearch?query=rc</a></li>
        <li><a href="/api/mcp/GetBaletteSourceFile?path=Demo/Client/Services/DemoCommands.cs" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/api/mcp/GetBaletteSourceFile?path=Demo/Client/Services/DemoCommands.cs</a></li>
    </ul>
</div>

@code {
    private const string ClientConfig = """
        // .mcp.json (Claude Code, VS Code, and anything else reading this shape)
        {
          "mcpServers": {
            "balette": {
              "type": "http",
              "url": "https://balette.bitplatform.dev/mcp"
            }
          }
        }
        """;
}
